// Failure golden: a nominal mismatch at a NESTED type position (ADR-80).
// (Pathological tree: testing artifact, not pedagogy -- ADR-52 Decision C.)
//
// `Celsius` and `Fahrenheit` are distinct generative-nominal types. A list of
// `Cel(20)` ascribed `List(Fahrenheit)` must be rejected -- the element `Cel`
// builds a `Celsius`, not the `Fahrenheit` the nested `List(...)` element type
// demands. This only fires if the declared datatype is rewritten to its nominal
// handle at DEPTH: a nested position that stayed structural (or holed) would
// let the mixup pass. It is the depth analogue of `nominal-distinctness`.
data Celsius { Cel(x: Integer) }
data Fahrenheit { Fah(x: Integer) }

([Cel(20)] : List(Fahrenheit))

//@ expect-diagnostic: Fahrenheit
